    [CI][Test] Skip the packed weight-update lanes on main (#18947)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Cherry-picks Ronald1995's test-only change from #18836, which
    temporarily skips the packed parametrizations of the NPU IPC and HCCL
    weight-transfer state-transition suites with a shared reason, while
    keeping the unpacked parametrizations enabled.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. Test-only change.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    ```bash
    pytest -sv -rs \
      tests/e2e/pull_request/one_card/rlhf/state_transitions/test_npu_ipc_weight_transfer.py \
      tests/e2e/pull_request/two_card/rlhf/state_transitions/test_hccl_weight_transfer.py \
      -k 'packed and not unpacked'
    ```
    
    Result: **6 skipped, 6 deselected**
    
    - Four Qwen3.5 / GLM-5.1 packed cases were skipped with the new shared
    reason referencing #18726 and #18763.
    - Two DeepSeek packed cases retained their existing model-specific skip.
    
    ---
    
    ### Checklist
    
    #### Testing
    
    - [x] **Boundary / edge-case coverage**: Not applicable; this is a
    test-only skip for an existing flaky parametrization.
    - [x] **Regression test**: Not applicable; the change temporarily
    disables the known-flaky packed lanes and preserves the unpacked
    coverage.
    - [x] **Error / failure path coverage**: Not applicable.
    - [x] **Meaningful & reliable tests**: Existing unpacked lanes remain
    enabled; the packed lanes report as skipped with a shared reason.
    - [x] **Performance impact**: Not applicable.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
